WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — satiation (45s) Narrator Gabriel

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:06.095
First, every job has a finish line, and extra computer work after that point is waste.

2
00:00:06.535 --> 00:00:13.262
Second, cheaper computer work makes people start many more jobs, so total use can keep rising.

3
00:00:13.702 --> 00:00:20.534
Third, money prices for AI are falling fast, but the electricity it burns is never free.

4
00:00:20.974 --> 00:00:27.321
Think of washing a dish: once the plate is clean, washing it ten more times wastes hot water.

5
00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:33.599
Yet when soap gets ten times cheaper, new restaurants open and total water use still climbs.

6
00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:39.990
Good software defines a clear written finish check and stops spending the instant a job is done,

7
00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:43.399
instead of mistaking endless chatter for real progress.
